; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ADDING A REAL-SQLITE COMPARISON EXECUTABLE?  READ THIS FIRST.  (#370, #574)
;
; Granary must not acquire a dependency on real SQLite, and CI enforces that
; with four greps over lib/ bin/ containers/ test/ bench/: one for the
; `"sqlite3 ..."` CLI error-string form, one for the OCaml `Sqlite3` module as
; a WHOLE WORD (so `open Sqlite3` and `module S = Sqlite3` are caught, not only
; the qualified form — #621), one against assembling that name from pieces
; (#605), and one over `dune` files and the root `dune-project` for the
; `(libraries ... sqlite3)` stanza that creates the dependency in the first
; place (#621).  Designated comparison files — the `(optional)` stanzas below
; that name `sqlite3`, or that shell out to the sqlite3 CLI — are allowlisted
; by path.  THIS FILE is allowlisted for the dune guard, so the guard says
; nothing about a stanza added here; the script explains why.
;
; The allowlists live in scripts/check-sqlite-policy.sh.  A new comparison
; file that is not listed there turns CI red on main even though it violates
; no policy; that has now happened twice (#505 for bench_tpch.ml, #500 for
; bench_tpcc.ml).  Add yours to the script in the same commit.
;
; The two lists are deliberately different sizes — shelling out to the CLI does
; not qualify a file to link the module.  The script explains why.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

